{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>At the entrance of Enaim.</b> At the convergence of two roads, for a road is called עַיִן (ʿayin), as in עַל הָעַיִן בְּדֶרֶךְ שׁוּר (Genesis 16:7)." "<b>Which is on the road to Timnah.</b> So that Judah would not escape encountering her on his way from Timnah." "<b>For she saw that Shelah had grown.</b> She reasoned that when Judah would see her deprived of her widow's garments and ask why she had done so, she would answer him that the time had come to remove them — for he had told her שְׁבִי אַלְמָנָה עַד יִגְדַּל שֵׁלָה (remain a widow until Shelah grows), and now Shelah had already grown."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:50.151307571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}